WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.319 --> 00:00:06.720
One of the things I find most curious about
Eiichiro Oda´s writing is the way he plays

00:00:06.720 --> 00:00:11.230
with established themes. If you are somewhat
familiar with One Piece, you will know that

00:00:11.230 --> 00:00:15.980
there are many elements in the story that
Oda borrows from outside sources and that

00:00:15.980 --> 00:00:21.529
often follow certain patterns. Some of these
themes serve as an underlying massage while

00:00:21.529 --> 00:00:27.230
others are simply a method of consistent storytelling.
Most stories make use of this principle and

00:00:27.230 --> 00:00:33.469
that inevitably leads to a general exhaustion
of many of these themes in contemporary works.

00:00:33.469 --> 00:00:39.470
Especially in fiction, we often find the same
ideas and elements recycled over and over

00:00:39.470 --> 00:00:44.739
again. What Oda does differently here is that
he integrates these widely spread ideas and

00:00:44.739 --> 00:00:50.090
takes them a step further. Some of them he
gives a twist while others he explores in

00:00:50.090 --> 00:00:55.650
a different context. A perfect example of
this method of writing is Sanji. Being one

00:00:55.650 --> 00:01:00.640
of the major figures of the series, Sanji
unites a whole bunch of ideas inside of his

00:01:00.640 --> 00:01:05.640
character. And following it can sometimes
feel like it is full of contradictions. In

00:01:05.640 --> 00:01:11.720
this video we will explore how Oda constructed
Sanji to be a true gentleman and how he subtly

00:01:11.720 --> 00:01:16.509
twists this stereotype in certain ways to
turn Sanji into a fascinating character that

00:01:16.509 --> 00:01:21.540
finds itself conflicted with its ideals and
values. In this context, we will also take

00:01:21.540 --> 00:01:26.680
a closer look at the true purpose of the Whole
Cake Island arc and discuss why our passionate

00:01:26.680 --> 00:01:29.910
cook is such an important part of the straw
hat crew.

00:01:29.910 --> 00:01:34.729
Before we can decide though if Sanji truly
is a gentleman, in every sense of the word,

00:01:34.729 --> 00:01:40.460
we must first understand what being a gentleman
actually means. The term ‘Gentleman’ nowadays

00:01:40.460 --> 00:01:46.020
is often confused for individual, superficial
acts of politeness. You sometimes hear guys

00:01:46.020 --> 00:01:51.320
being called a gentleman for basically not
behaving like an asshole. But being a gentleman

00:01:51.320 --> 00:01:56.140
has nothing to do with holding open the door
for a woman nor with being a man. It is much

00:01:56.140 --> 00:02:01.990
rather determined by a person´s overall behavior
and mindset. Becoming a gentleman is something

00:02:01.990 --> 00:02:07.220
than takes a strong conviction as well as
a lot of time and effort. There are a whole

00:02:07.220 --> 00:02:13.420
bunch of qualities that make a true gentleman.
These include chivalry, compassion and kindness,

00:02:13.420 --> 00:02:19.300
respect, bravery, loyalty and cleverness.
Being a gentleman therefore means being respectful

00:02:19.300 --> 00:02:23.670
and tolerant in interactions with others,
while putting their interests before your

00:02:23.670 --> 00:02:27.840
own. Why would anyone want to go through all
that in the first place though?

00:02:27.840 --> 00:02:32.790
There are several reasons why it might be
worth to strive for becoming a gentleman.

00:02:32.790 --> 00:02:37.700
Obviously, it comes with a certain amount
of altruism and finding pleasure in helping

00:02:37.700 --> 00:02:42.850
others. This can mean helping and protecting
those who are in need or important to you,

00:02:42.850 --> 00:02:47.700
bringing positivity and kindness into someone´s
life or simply inspiring others to follow

00:02:47.700 --> 00:02:52.700
your example for creating a more social and
positive environment. But of course, it also

00:02:52.700 --> 00:02:57.400
holds benefits for you personally: Behaving
in a gentleman-like manner towards others

00:02:57.400 --> 00:03:02.650
will earn you the respect and trust of those
around you. This again will in the end inspire

00:03:02.650 --> 00:03:07.640
more positive behavior back towards yourself
as well, creating a kind of positive feedback

00:03:07.640 --> 00:03:12.400
loop for everyone involved. If you spin this
thought even further and look at it from a

00:03:12.400 --> 00:03:17.320
cultural perspective, encouraging such behavior
may in the end result in a more considerate

00:03:17.320 --> 00:03:22.870
and healthy society, one that actively seeks
to be helpful. Helpful in a genuine, open

00:03:22.870 --> 00:03:28.260
and kind way, and not in a patronizing or
superior way. In other words, a gentleman,

00:03:28.260 --> 00:03:33.820
and that can be anyone, is someone that unites
a broad variety of positive characteristics

00:03:33.820 --> 00:03:38.150
that benefit those around them.
On the other hand, what you probably are also

00:03:38.150 --> 00:03:42.430
aware of though, is the fact that characters
who are through and through good, are usually

00:03:42.430 --> 00:03:46.890
not the ones we love and root for the most
in a story and we will later on also explore

00:03:46.890 --> 00:03:51.511
what problems such a white knight can bring
with it in the context of storytelling. Since

00:03:51.511 --> 00:03:56.190
people in the real world are not that black
or white, we tend to prefer characters that

00:03:56.190 --> 00:04:00.580
are morally a little bit more gray.
So now, let´s take a look, weather Sanji

00:04:00.580 --> 00:04:05.780
actually fulfills the requirements to be called
a true gentleman, what implications that has

00:04:05.780 --> 00:04:10.800
for his character and why he is so essential
to the story. Quick disclaimer at this point:

00:04:10.800 --> 00:04:14.790
If you aren´t caught up with the story of
One Piece yet be careful, because from now

00:04:14.790 --> 00:04:19.040
on this video will contain spoilers for Sanji´s
character arc.

00:04:19.040 --> 00:04:23.500
Being part of the monster trio and one of
the early members of the crew, Sanji is one

00:04:23.500 --> 00:04:27.890
of the most beloved characters in the story.
While his considerable fighting abilities

00:04:27.890 --> 00:04:33.200
as well as his cool and collected manner play
a big part in this, Sanji´s character has

00:04:33.200 --> 00:04:38.710
a high level of complexity and therefore has
a lot more to offer. Over the years we have

00:04:38.710 --> 00:04:43.150
gotten to know Sanji better and better and
with the events at Whole Cake Island, we now

00:04:43.150 --> 00:04:48.110
finally have a very full picture of why Sanji
became the person he is today. So now, let´s

00:04:48.110 --> 00:04:53.000
take a look at the five defining character
traits for Sanji, and how they qualify him

00:04:53.000 --> 00:04:58.770
to be the true gentleman of the story:
The first trait that we will look at is Sanji´s

00:04:58.770 --> 00:05:03.500
cleverness. While inside the monster trio
he might not be considered quite as powerful

00:05:03.500 --> 00:05:09.420
as Luffy or Zoro by some, he often makes up
for it by fighting smarter. Sanji often finds

00:05:09.420 --> 00:05:15.010
himself wandering off alone during large encounters,
only to discover secret doors and weaknesses

00:05:15.010 --> 00:05:20.130
that he is able to exploit for the crew's
benefit. His curiosity and cleverness often

00:05:20.130 --> 00:05:25.200
put him into situations where he is able to
save the rest of his crew. Sanji does so on

00:05:25.200 --> 00:05:30.680
the way to Alabasta, posing as Mr. 3 and giving
the crew a decisive edge against Crocodile

00:05:30.680 --> 00:05:35.670
as he is unknown to the Baroque Works organization.
Later on, when the rest of the crew was captured

00:05:35.670 --> 00:05:41.080
on Alabasta, Sanji outwitted him again using
a Den Den Mushi. He then repeats this feat

00:05:41.080 --> 00:05:46.470
in Skypeia to wreak havoc on Enel's ship from
the inside. When Robin was captured by the

00:05:46.470 --> 00:05:51.640
CP9 at Water7, Sanji already figured, they
would take her to the station and waited for

00:05:51.640 --> 00:05:56.070
them there. And later, on Enies Lobby, he
went off on his own in order to close the

00:05:56.070 --> 00:06:00.990
Gates of Justice much rather than engaging
with the guards on the island. In Punk Hazard,

00:06:00.990 --> 00:06:05.610
he left the group in order to save Tashigi
from Vergo. But the most significant case

00:06:05.610 --> 00:06:10.690
would most likely be having to leave Zou to
spare his crew from Big Moms wrath by going

00:06:10.690 --> 00:06:16.120
and confronting his family. All these examples
show how Sanji uses his cleverness in critical

00:06:16.120 --> 00:06:21.550
situations to turn the tables for his crew
mates. But we can also see Sanji´s cleverness

00:06:21.550 --> 00:06:26.250
outside of battles. He is usually very perceptive
of things and seems to have a good judgement

00:06:26.250 --> 00:06:32.100
when it comes to critical situations. Being
clever is essential to being a true gentleman,

00:06:32.100 --> 00:06:36.830
because understanding situations and people
and knowing how to act appropriately, is an

00:06:36.830 --> 00:06:40.030
important trait in order to have a positive
influence.

00:06:40.030 --> 00:06:46.220
The second important characteristic is Sanji´s
deep sense of compassion and kindness. Sanji

00:06:46.220 --> 00:06:51.561
might be one of the kindest and most empathetic
characters in all of One Piece. While we usually

00:06:51.561 --> 00:06:56.480
see Sanji carrying himself in a very calm,
cool, and collected manner, he is not someone

00:06:56.480 --> 00:07:02.680
to be afraid of showing emotion and weakness
from time to time. We have seen many characters

00:07:02.680 --> 00:07:08.389
admiring Sanji´s kind heart including his
mother, his sister, Luffy and even Brook,

00:07:08.389 --> 00:07:13.950
who stated: “Sanji is just too Kind! Once
he decides to protect someone, he will put

00:07:13.950 --> 00:07:17.740
his life on the line for them!” Despite
growing up under the terror of his father

00:07:17.740 --> 00:07:22.990
and his brothers, Sanji always kept his strong
sense of compassion and generosity. After

00:07:22.990 --> 00:07:27.590
he was taken in by Zeff, these attributes
were imbued deep into his personality and

00:07:27.590 --> 00:07:32.560
define a lot of Sanji´s decisions and actions
throughout the story. Next to the people closest

00:07:32.560 --> 00:07:37.120
to him, that he would go to any length to,
in order to save them and make them happy,

00:07:37.120 --> 00:07:42.180
he also cares for strangers. This can be seen
on various occasions, when Sanji goes out

00:07:42.180 --> 00:07:48.060
of his way to save Gin at the Baratie, Kin’emon
and Tashigi on Punk Hazard, the Minks on Zou

00:07:48.060 --> 00:07:52.860
as well as Chiffon from Oven´s wrath on Whole
Cake Island. He even refused to leave his

00:07:52.860 --> 00:07:57.430
family behind that caused him so much agony
and pain in his childhood and that had made

00:07:57.430 --> 00:08:02.520
use of him to get close to Big Mom. And he
also protected Pudding at the wedding ceremony,

00:08:02.520 --> 00:08:07.389
despite being aware of her true intentions.
As you can see, Sanji cares for friends and

00:08:07.389 --> 00:08:12.360
foes alike when a situation calls for empathy
and compassion. But his kindness probably

00:08:12.360 --> 00:08:17.240
is most pronounced in his rule to never let
anyone go hungry, no matter who they might

00:08:17.240 --> 00:08:22.930
be. After having expernienced true hunger
himself, he swore to himself to not let anyone

00:08:22.930 --> 00:08:28.080
go through that, if he can help it. His desire
to help and protect others is a central part

00:08:28.080 --> 00:08:32.510
of being a gentleman and Sanji lives by this
ideal without a second thought.

00:08:32.510 --> 00:08:38.860
The third personality trait that is defining
for Sanji´s character are loyalty and respect.

00:08:38.860 --> 00:08:44.480
Similar to Zoro, Sanji also strongly believes
in loyalty. Not only would Sanji do anything

00:08:44.480 --> 00:08:49.490
for those he loves, but he also sided with
Zoro about Usopp rejoining the crew when the

00:08:49.490 --> 00:08:54.529
latter stepped on Luffy's pride. It was therefore
so much worse for him, when he was the one

00:08:54.529 --> 00:09:00.260
to betray Luffy and the crew later on Zou.
Obviously, it was a hard blow to his self-esteem

00:09:00.260 --> 00:09:04.750
when he was faced with the choice between
leaving the crew or the life of his matter-of-fact

00:09:04.750 --> 00:09:09.740
father Zeff. The internal conflict that this
decision had engulfed Sanji in, resulted in

00:09:09.740 --> 00:09:14.400
a lot of pain for everyone involved. Sanji
even claimed that he had lost the right to

00:09:14.400 --> 00:09:19.380
return to the crew, until Luffy convinced
him otherwise. This already shows us one of

00:09:19.380 --> 00:09:23.881
the problems with Sanji´s strong ideals,
but we will get back to that in a bit. Hand

00:09:23.881 --> 00:09:29.660
in hand with Sanji´s loyalty goes a strong
sense for respect. This obviously includes

00:09:29.660 --> 00:09:35.540
respect for Zeff, his captain and crew mates,
but also respect for certain enemies. And

00:09:35.540 --> 00:09:40.810
of course, Sanji requires respect from anyone,
when it comes to food and women. We can see

00:09:40.810 --> 00:09:45.630
the full extent of his respect and loyalty
on Thriller Bark when he tries to scarify

00:09:45.630 --> 00:09:52.170
himself for his captain, before Zoro steps
in and knocks him out to take on that responsibility.

00:09:52.170 --> 00:09:57.110
Loyal and respectful behavior are more than
necessary features to be considered a gentleman

00:09:57.110 --> 00:10:00.339
after all.
The next critical trait for Sanji are his

00:10:00.339 --> 00:10:06.240
bravery and combat attitude. Without a doubt
we know that Sanji is strong. While there

00:10:06.240 --> 00:10:10.710
is always a lot of debate going on over how
everyone ranks in the crew strength wise,

00:10:10.710 --> 00:10:15.160
I think no one will disagree that Sanji is
one of the most important combatants of the

00:10:15.160 --> 00:10:20.149
crew. Usually being fearless in battle, he
is often seen fighting armies and powerful

00:10:20.149 --> 00:10:24.580
opponents with barely more than a concerned
look. And being part of the monster trio,

00:10:24.580 --> 00:10:29.920
he usually ends up fighting one of the stronger
opponents in an arc. Despite having significant

00:10:29.920 --> 00:10:35.500
battle skills though different from Luffy
or Zoro, he usually tries to avoid a confrontation

00:10:35.500 --> 00:10:41.240
whenever possible. And while we see him enjoying
a battle at times, Sanji usually only enters

00:10:41.240 --> 00:10:47.540
a battle to protect or help someone else.
On Thriller Bark he fights Absalom to protect

00:10:47.540 --> 00:10:52.770
Nami. And just recently in Wano, he immediately
jumped in to protect Toko from Shogun Orochi´s

00:10:52.770 --> 00:10:57.520
attempt to kill her, standing side by side
with Zoro. Having the wish AND the ability

00:10:57.520 --> 00:11:02.720
to fight for and protect others, are important
assets for a gentleman after all.

00:11:02.720 --> 00:11:07.460
Lastly, we have to take a look at Sanji´s
chivalry, which in general is an essential

00:11:07.460 --> 00:11:13.480
part of being a gentleman but has two different
sides in Sanji´s case. In some cases, Sanji

00:11:13.480 --> 00:11:18.550
can be seen acting mature and cool around
women, further supporting his image as a gentleman.

00:11:18.550 --> 00:11:24.150
In other cases though, it can get very excessive
and pervy. Some people think that his perverted

00:11:24.150 --> 00:11:29.150
nature is taken too far and often crosses
the line of being comedic and sometimes even

00:11:29.150 --> 00:11:33.710
to downright creepy. And while I don´t disagree
with that, it´s something that in a manga

00:11:33.710 --> 00:11:38.230
you maybe have to accept as a quirk to the
character. I personally don´t think that

00:11:38.230 --> 00:11:42.630
Sanji should lose this side of him completely,
but I think it would allow more people to

00:11:42.630 --> 00:11:47.211
see him as a great character, if it were to
be tuned down a little. That being said, over

00:11:47.211 --> 00:11:51.630
the course of the story, this has somewhat
improved, especially by giving Sanji some

00:11:51.630 --> 00:11:56.080
real experiences with women, like Viola or
Pudding, that helped him maturing a little

00:11:56.080 --> 00:12:01.070
in that regard. This excessive behavior aside
though, Sanji in general has a very respectful

00:12:01.070 --> 00:12:06.250
and chivalrous attitude towards woman. This
even goes so far that next to feeding anyone

00:12:06.250 --> 00:12:11.700
who is hungry, Sanji’s second big rule in
life is not to hurt or fight women. This attitude

00:12:11.700 --> 00:12:16.279
most likely developed under the influence
of his sister Reiju, who was his only positive

00:12:16.279 --> 00:12:21.780
influence in his childhood as well as Zeff,
who held strong ideals himself. As a result,

00:12:21.780 --> 00:12:27.430
he becomes infuriated with anyone going against
this ideal. This can for example be seen inside

00:12:27.430 --> 00:12:32.160
the Germa´s castle. When he found Cosette
brutally beaten to the point of unconsciousness,

00:12:32.160 --> 00:12:38.301
Sanji became absolutely furious. He went on
to find Niki and ended up braking jaw, all

00:12:38.301 --> 00:12:41.970
that despite the threats and warnings his
family issued towards him.

00:12:41.970 --> 00:12:47.691
All these qualities, his cleverness, his compassion
and kindness, his loyalty and respect, his

00:12:47.691 --> 00:12:53.130
bravery as well as his chivalry, make Sanji
into a true gentleman. Someone that the people

00:12:53.130 --> 00:12:59.209
around him can rely on. What then is the problem
with this codex that Sanji follows? And how

00:12:59.209 --> 00:13:04.070
did it affect his character, not only story
wise, but also in the eyes of many fans?

00:13:04.070 --> 00:13:08.880
Like all of the other straw hats, Sanji also
follows a dream for which he joined Luffy

00:13:08.880 --> 00:13:14.130
on his journey: Finding the legendary all
blue, a sea where fish from all over the world

00:13:14.130 --> 00:13:18.330
are gathered together. What makes this dream
so much different from all of the other straw

00:13:18.330 --> 00:13:22.740
hats´ though, is that this is not really
a dream that you can truly make any tangible

00:13:22.740 --> 00:13:27.750
progress towards over the course of the journey.
Finding a place is different from becoming

00:13:27.750 --> 00:13:32.440
stronger or better at what you do. And we
also pretty much never see Sanji making any

00:13:32.440 --> 00:13:36.980
active efforts to find out more about his
dream. So, in other words, his development

00:13:36.980 --> 00:13:42.220
over the story is usually more for other people
than for himself. Sanji doesn´t have the

00:13:42.220 --> 00:13:47.070
motivation to become stronger just for the
sake of it. His goal is completely unrelated

00:13:47.070 --> 00:13:52.330
to his character. What Sanji strives for much
rather, is to uphold his ideals and be a true

00:13:52.330 --> 00:13:57.620
gentleman. A knight on a white horse. While
this in its own way is also a very difficult

00:13:57.620 --> 00:14:02.750
and noble task, in a story like One Piece
that not only is focused around personal growth

00:14:02.750 --> 00:14:07.570
but also is incredibly long, it can be difficult
to cheer for a character, that strives for

00:14:07.570 --> 00:14:12.410
staying the same, rather than changing. We
enjoy seeing Luffy training to get new skills

00:14:12.410 --> 00:14:17.060
and Zoro learning new techniques. What is
easy to overlook though, is Sanji´s struggle

00:14:17.060 --> 00:14:22.310
with his morality and values. Having a list
of rules to live by, some might argue that

00:14:22.310 --> 00:14:27.670
this works against the character. If he never
breaks that rule, then how can there be conflict?

00:14:27.670 --> 00:14:33.110
How can that character not seem static and
boring? But that is simply not true. Sanji´s

00:14:33.110 --> 00:14:39.170
curse is that he is always compared to Zoro
and Luffy, since he has comparable fighting

00:14:39.170 --> 00:14:43.980
power. There is the strong expectation for
him to similarly strive for more strength.

00:14:43.980 --> 00:14:48.910
But I think it is important to realize that
Sanji´s personality and character arc are

00:14:48.910 --> 00:14:54.040
just extremely different from these two. One
Piece is after all not only a story about

00:14:54.040 --> 00:14:58.470
characters being changed by the world, it
is in many ways also a story about the world

00:14:58.470 --> 00:15:04.730
being changed by the characters. Sanji again
and again comes into conflict with his ideals.

00:15:04.730 --> 00:15:09.350
His conviction to not fight women under any
circumstances, often hinders him from helping

00:15:09.350 --> 00:15:14.450
and protecting those around him. This can
be seen in his fight against Kalifa from CP9

00:15:14.450 --> 00:15:18.980
during the Enies Lobby arc. And the conflict
between his loyalty towards Zeff and his loyalty

00:15:18.980 --> 00:15:23.620
towards his crew end up in the Whole Cake
Island arc, which´s purpose has been deeply

00:15:23.620 --> 00:15:28.040
misunderstood exactly for that same reason.
People thought that the arc was all about

00:15:28.040 --> 00:15:32.550
Sanji getting stronger, catching up to Luffy
and Zoro and there was a lot of disappointment

00:15:32.550 --> 00:15:37.490
when that didn´t happen. But as we just saw,
that´s not what this character is about.

00:15:37.490 --> 00:15:42.600
Whole Cake Island was Sanji´s arc, because
his ideals, that he strives to keep up finally

00:15:42.600 --> 00:15:47.269
pushed him into a moral corner, where he had
no choice but change. He had to experience

00:15:47.269 --> 00:15:51.079
the problems and pain that sticking to his
ideals could mean and he had to learn and

00:15:51.079 --> 00:15:55.180
accept to trust his captain and his crew in
order to be able to keep them alive in the

00:15:55.180 --> 00:16:00.500
future. In other words, Sanji had to grow
as a character to stay loyal to his values.

00:16:00.500 --> 00:16:04.329
So, the next time you read the Whole Cake
Island arc, I ask you to keep that in mind

00:16:04.329 --> 00:16:09.360
and try to look at the events from that perspective.
You will see that the entire arc gets an entirely

00:16:09.360 --> 00:16:13.510
new gravity for Sanji´s character, when you
stop looking at him the same way you look

00:16:13.510 --> 00:16:17.279
at Zoro or Luffy.
Sanji is such a fascinating character, because

00:16:17.279 --> 00:16:21.890
his personality and his combat skills make
his character seem inconsistent and contradictive

00:16:21.890 --> 00:16:26.410
at times. But it is important to realize how
great it is for the straw hat crew, to have

00:16:26.410 --> 00:16:30.829
someone as kind and compassionate as Sanji
on the crew, that also has the power to act

00:16:30.829 --> 00:16:35.950
upon it. So, despite being close to Luffy
and Zoro in terms of combat ability, his character

00:16:35.950 --> 00:16:41.250
arc is very different and unique inside the
crew. Being a true gentleman brings many challenges

00:16:41.250 --> 00:16:46.120
and hardships with it, but it also makes Sanji
so incredibly important for the crew and the

00:16:46.120 --> 00:16:51.090
entire story. Plus, he can cook. What else
could anyone ask for?

00:16:51.090 --> 00:16:56.019
Hey everybody. Thank you so much for watching.
I feel like there often is a lot of competition

00:16:56.019 --> 00:17:01.020
between Sanji and Zoro fans. But I personally
think that there is no issue in loving both

